331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 282 0 R
/T ([III] What are the Goals of the Tradewinds Solutions Marketplace?)
/E ([III] What are the Goals of the Tradewinds Solutions Marketplace?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 282 0 R
/T (The goals of the Tradewinds Solutions Marketplace are to establish a centralized location where DoW can assess the state of the art in available AI/ML, digital, and data solutions, and where industry, academia, and individual solution providers can promote their research, technologies, and related products and services to the government. Further, the structure of the solicitation and assessment functions of the Marketplace allow for streamlined procurement of available solutions, addressing an impediment to large business, small business, traditional and nontraditional contractors, and research institutions. Finally, by leveraging the statutory and regulatory authorities available, the Solutions Marketplace model provides technology transition pathways from idea to research, research to prototype, prototype to test and evaluation, through production, fielding, and sustainment of a given solution.)
/E (The goals of the Tradewinds Solutions Marketplace are to establish a centralized location where DoW can assess the state of the art in available AI/ML, digital, and data solutions, and where industry, academia, and individual solution providers can promote their research, technologies, and related products and services to the government. Further, the structure of the solicitation and assessment functions of the Marketplace allow for streamlined procurement of available solutions, addressing an impediment to large business, small business, traditional and nontraditional contractors, and research institutions. Finally, by leveraging the statutory and regulatory authorities available, the Solutions Marketplace model provides technology transition pathways from idea to research, research to prototype, prototype to test and evaluation, through production, fielding, and sustainment of a given solution.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
