/Title (a.   A significant potential conflict exists as to SME assessors evaluating their own technology solutions. The government will avoid this potential OCI by prohibiting assessors from evaluating their own technology solutions, or the solutions of another submitter in which the assessor holds any financial interest from their contract requirements. Further, the government will mitigate any potential OCI by prohibiting assessors to evaluate their own technology solutions, or the solutions of another submitter in which the assessor holds any financial interest and requiring assessors to deliver a statement certifying that they recognize this prohibition, including an affirmative duty to identify any such financial interests. All assessors will be required to complete government ethics training, covering this duty to identify financial interests, prior to assessing any solution submissions and will operate under nondisclosure agreements to protect any information received through the assessment activity.)
